+      "observation": "get_parser() is the single option-declaration entry point. It builds a configargparse.ArgumentParser with YAMLConfigFileParser and auto_env_var_prefix='AIDER_' (lines 36-42), meaning a single declaration layer feeds CLI flags, YAML config files and AIDER_* environment variables. All groups (main model, API keys, model/cache/repomap, output, git, lint/test, analytics, upgrade, modes, voice, other, deprecated) are registered here and the assembled parser is returned at line 869, to be reused for parsing, help generation and shtab completion."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/args.py",
+      "symbol": "edit_format_choices",
+      "start_line": 48,
+      "end_line": 57,
+      "observation": "edit_format_choices is computed dynamically from the registered coder classes in aider.coders (`{c.edit_format ...}`), then used as the argparse `choices=` set for --edit-format/--chat-mode (lines 163-171) and --editor-edit-format. This makes invalid edit formats fail during argparse validation while keeping the allowed set in sync with the coder registry."
