+      "end_line": 303,
+      "observation": "parse_lint_cmds() is a runtime validator/transformer for the append-style --lint-cmd values: it splits `lang: cmd` pairs, strips whitespace, reports a descriptive error and returns None on malformed/empty commands. main.py (line 885) treats a None result as a fatal configuration error and returns exit code 1, i.e. validation continues after argparse."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/main.py",
+      "symbol": "main",
+      "start_line": 451,
+      "end_line": 1181,
+      "observation": "main() is the orchestration pipeline: it guesses git_root (454-461), assembles default_config_files in cwd/git-root/home order (463-477), then performs a three-stage parse. First get_parser + parse_known_args for the initial guess (479-487), then rebuilds the parser with the reversed config-file order and parse_known_args again (494-498), loads .env (501), and finally parser.parse_args(argv) (504) so CLI/cwd values win over later config sources. After parsing it applies post-parse runtime configuration: --shell-completions early-exit (506-510), dark/light mode color+theme overrides (532-548), --set-env and --api-key env-var side effects with format validation (590-612), API-key env exports and deprecated-arg handling (614-632). Because the true repo may differ from the guess, it recurses into main() with force_git_root when guessed_wrong_repo disagrees (717-720)."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/main.py",
+      "symbol": "get_io",
+      "start_line": 551,
+      "end_line": 578,
+      "observation": "The nested get_io() closes over the parsed args to construct the runtime InputOutput object (colors, history files, edit mode, encoding, line endings, notifications, dry-run, etc.). main.py calls it as `io = get_io(args.pretty)` at line 580 and re-creates a non-pretty IO on UnicodeEncodeError, showing that runtime configuration is materialized from the namespace after post-parse mutation."
+    },
+    {
+      "path": "aider/main.py",
+      "symbol": "Coder.create",
+      "start_line": 973,
+      "end_line": 1020,
+      "observation": "Coder.create() is the final runtime-configuration assembly point: nearly every relevant parsed attribute (edit_format, show_diffs, auto_commits, map_tokens, lint_cmds, test_cmd, map_refresh, cache_prompts, languages, copy-paste, accept-architect, add-gitignore-files) is threaded into the coder, with UnknownEditFormat/ValueError caught and converted into a diagnostic exit. The same factory is reused inside the SwitchCoder loop (line 1177) to rebuild configuration mid-session."
+    }
+  ],
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "claim": "Option parsing for aider is centralized in aider/args.py:get_parser, which constructs a single configargparse YAML-aware parser with auto_env_var_prefix='AIDER_' so the same option declarations serve CLI flags, .aider.conf.yml config files, and AIDER_* environment variables.",
