+      "evidence_paths": ["aider/main.py"]
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "Post-parse runtime configuration in aider/main.py mutates the parsed namespace and process environment: dark/light-mode color and code-theme overrides, --set-env and --api-key writes to os.environ with format-error exits, and OPENAI_*/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY exports including deprecated-flag handling.",
+      "evidence_paths": ["aider/main.py"]
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "Runtime configuration is materialized from the parsed namespace by aider/main.py:get_io (InputOutput construction) and Coder.create (coder construction), with parse-time options plus derived values (map_tokens from the model, lint_cmds from parse_lint_cmds) threaded through; UnknownEditFormat/ValueError are converted into exit code 1 rather than tracebacks.",
+      "evidence_paths": ["aider/main.py"]
+    },
+    {
+      "claim": "aider/main.py handles misconfiguration gracefully: check_config_files_for_yes turns a legacy `yes:` config key's AttributeError into an actionable message, and when the guessed git root differs from the real repository main() recurses with force_git_root so config/history paths are re-resolved in the correct context.",
+      "evidence_paths": ["aider/main.py"]
+    }
+  ],
+  "conclusion": "The option-parsing surface of aider is a single declarative layer in aider/args.py:get_parser. It uses configargparse with a YAML config-file parser and the AIDER_ env-var prefix, so one set of declarations simultaneously defines CLI flags, config-file keys and environment variables; parse-time validation is enforced via argparse choices/types (notably the dynamically derived edit_format_choices and the resolve_aiderignore_path type= callable), and deprecated model flags are appended before the parser is returned. aider/main.py:main then drives the option namespace through validation into runtime configuration in three stages: (1) it guesses the git root and builds the default_config_files search list (cwd, git root, home) passed to get_parser; (2) it performs a multi-pass parse - an initial parse_known_args that tolerates unknown options, a .env load between passes, a re-build with the config-file order reversed, and a final strict parse_args - so that CLI/earlier sources win and diagnostic handlers (check_config_files_for_yes) can catch bad config; and (3) it applies post-parse runtime configuration, including dark/light-mode overrides, --set-env/--api-key os.environ side effects, API-key exports, deprecated-arg handling, and semantic validation such as parse_lint_cmds. Finally it materializes runtime objects via the nested get_io() (InputOutput) and Coder.create(), converting configuration errors (malformed --set-env/--api-key/--lint-cmd, UnknownEditFormat, model-metadata failures) into descriptive messages and exit code 1, and recursing with force_git_root when the real repo differs from the initial guess. Overall the flow is: declarative option map (args.py) -> multi-pass parse plus diagnostic recovery -> key-specific overrides and environment side effects -> runtime objects (io, coder) in main.py.",
